   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the city of Albany to discontinue the use of certain lands as park lands",
    "basePrintNo": "S7606",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7606-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7606\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto authorize the city of Albany to discontinue the use of\ncertain lands as park lands\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo allow the City of Albany to\nalienate a small under utilized pocket park and sell it so that it can\nbe developed and the property put back on the tax rolls.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 - authorization of the alienation\n\nSection 2 - delineates the property to be alienated\n\nSection 3 - describes the park land that will replace the alienated\nproperty\n\nSection 4 - effective date\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nTo allow the city to replace a small pocket park -where the majority\nof the property is well below street level and contains forest and\novergrowth- to sell it so it can be developed into independent senior\ngarden apartments. The city will dedicate new city park lands of\nequal or greater fair market value to the lands being alienated.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
